# Ruling: "An opus ability resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger. It resolves even if that spell is countered or
# otherwise leaves the stack." Bot1 casts Mind Twist for X = 4 (five mana) on turn 3; with the opus trigger above it on the stack,
# Bot2 counters Mind Twist with Counterspell. The trigger then resolves with the spell gone: the five mana spent, judged as the spell
# last was (CR 608.2h), still makes a copy, and the Stallion is a 4/4. Mind Twist did nothing: Bot2 discards no card.

